A||N||17||mblackwell||My Fiero:Impounded||||8||
Z||000000||mblackwell||08-02-2001||09:19 PM||||Yesterday, I was driving to one of the local elementary schools to do some computer work.  On the way there I picked up some Wendy's for me and my cow-orker.<P>While I was passing through the town of Ashville, I noticed that one of the the town's three police cars was behind me.  It seemed to be following me.  It was.<P>It turns out my plates expired in February, and I was too stupid to notice.  They towed my Fiero to a lot behind the post office.  They pulled it with the back wheels on the ground, is that the way you are supposed to do it?<P>Now I hafta go buy new plates, and then pay some huge ransom to get my car back.  Then after that I have to go to court.  GRRRR  Its a Mayer's court, so the only pleas they can accept are Guilty, and No Contest.  I guess if it goes badly I'll change my plea to not guilty so the case will go to the real court.  The judge there is pretty cool.<P>THe whole thing really pisses me off though, GRRRRRRRRR.<P>Another thing, the cruiser had video and radar systems, but no freakin cup holders for my Wendy's drinks.<P>I hope to get her back saturday.<p>[This message has been edited by mblackwell (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||JayUSA77||08-02-2001||09:24 PM||||well at least you got to sit in the front seat <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||mblackwell||08-02-2001||09:35 PM||||Nope, I was in the back.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||08-02-2001||09:36 PM||||Towing with the back wheels on the ground is only bad for an Automatic. Even then it's only a problem if it's for a long distance (20 miles or more???). If they only have 3 cop cars I doubt the post office is far from ANYWHERE in town so it should be just fine even if its an auto.<P>Good luck with the judge... Plead stupidity, and apologize profusely. Most won't be too harsh if they believe it was REALLY an oversight...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-02-2001||09:52 PM||||Plead no contest. You know it expired so your really guilty. On no contest mitigating circumstances may bring the fine down. No contest means the judge decides what the fine is or if there is any at all. If your records clean, you could get off with a warning.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mblackwell||08-02-2001||09:55 PM||||I hope so, I have almost no money.  I wish a cop would have noticed it when it was only expired for a short time.  They wouldn't have towed it then.||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||08-02-2001||11:16 PM||||There's usually a single cupholder up front in the center console. Just behind the light and siren controls. I can't believe he didn't offer to keep your food up front for you! I would have, except I wouldn't be responsible for missing evidence-uh I mean food! LOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever2||08-02-2001||11:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>no freakin cup holders<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Oh, like your Fiero has any?!<P>Did you give your fries to the K-9 dog?<P>But seriously, I'm sorry for the fate of your Fiero.  I sure hope nobody messes with it there in the impound lot.  It happens.  Maybe that's where the FieroCam should be.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||mblackwell||08-02-2001||11:44 PM||||My Fiero was equipped with two cup holders from the factory.  They are sized perfectly, Wendy's biggie drinks fit in them perfectly.  The condensation does drip on my legs, though.  The 'cup holders' are located on either side of the gauge cluster housing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Steve Normington||08-03-2001||12:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mblackwell:<BR><B>The 'cup holders' are located on either side of the gauge cluster housing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How many doughnuts?||||reg||1
Z||000010||maryjane||08-03-2001||01:06 AM||||You might try to contact whoever you have to face in court and get the date moved up as soon as possible to keep the storage fees down. They can mount up pretty quick. When I first got our 84 auto, the ign mod in the distrib went out the first time we took it out of town. I towed it back with jeep, under 30mph and only about 18 miles in distance. Never had a bit of trouble w/transmission. Been 5 yrs(Knock on wooden desktop)Good luck in court||||reg||1
Z||000011||mblackwell||08-03-2001||01:22 AM||||Doughnuts?  <P>I think those go on the shifter, but I have an auto so they won't fit.||||reg||1
Z||000012||mblackwell||08-03-2001||01:24 AM||||I can get the car out before I go to court.  I just have to buy the tags and go get it.  I cant get to the BMV 'til saturday though. I think storage is $8 per day.||||reg||1
Z||000013||maryjane||08-03-2001||01:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mblackwell:<BR><B>I can get the car out before I go to court.  I just have to buy the tags and go get it.  I cant get to the BMV 'til saturday though. I think storage is $8 per day.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>That's cheap, it's around $30/day here & if you'd had donuts it might not be impounded <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
